  "body": "Urban Chic, Serene Quiet | A Study In Leaf-filtered Light\r\n\r\nDistinctive architecture, light-filled interiors and a beautifully established private garden make this a refreshingly different proposition in the heart of Takapuna.\r\n\r\nOffering a generous floor area across three levels, this characterful home offers the convenience of traditional townhouse-style living with the space, individuality and outdoor enjoyment of an established residence.\r\n\r\nThe main living area is bright, airy and welcoming, with striking black-framed glazing, polished concrete floors and a lovely connection to the outside. Large windows draw in natural light and greenery, while doors open directly to a wonderfully private courtyard garden. Framed by mature planting, with a combination of paving and decking, the sheltered outdoor spaces are a particularly appealing feature. Whether enjoying a quiet morning coffee, entertaining friends or simply relaxing amongst the greenery, it offers a peaceful retreat remarkably close to the centre of Takapuna.\r\n\r\nThe contemporary kitchen is both practical and attractive, with generous bench space, fresh cabinetry and a tiled splashback. It enjoys immediate access to the elevated balcony, providing an inviting place to sit outdoors, enjoy the outlook or catch up with friends.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, two well-proportioned bedrooms are graced by excellent natural light, complemented by the large airy main bathroom. There is the convenience of another downstairs. Two heat pumps provide year-round comfort.\r\n\r\nAdding considerably to the property's versatility is a substantial additional room on the lower level. Offering a large additional multipurpose space, ideal as an office or rumpus area for hobbies or creative pursuits, it is an appealing bonus beyond the home's two bedrooms and has been sound-proofed to provide the ultimate flexibility if you have a gamer in the household or perhaps a music lover.\r\n\r\nA high-stud, internal-access garage provides secure parking and valuable space for bikes, sporting equipment and storage.\r\n\r\nBeyond the home, the location is exceptional. Takapuna's vibrant cafes, restaurants, shops, entertainment and beautiful beach are all within walking distance, with public transport and major commuter routes also conveniently accessible. The address is zoned for Takapuna School, Takapuna Normal Intermediate School, Takapuna Grammar School and Westlake Girls' High School.\r\n\r\nWith its distinctive design, generous proportions, unexpectedly private outdoor spaces and superb central location, 4/16 Huron Street offers an appealing alternative to conventional living and with its established garden, extensive glazing, genuinely generous floor area and quiet elegance.\r\n\r\nIf your ambitions for your daily life include walking a waterside suburb, local shopping and then returning home to read, draw, and dream, this is the sweetly private, beautifully kept residence for you. \r\n\r\nContact Anna Sareczky on 021 607 971 to arrange your viewing.\r\n\r\nSet date of sale 5pm Wednesday 4 November (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nAgents, conjunctional arrangements will be warmly welcomed. \r\n\r\nNote: school zone information was obtained from https://boundfor.co.nz/school-zones/auckland",
